\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Impulse responses to a $+1\sigma $ German cost-push shock $\eta _{p,F}$ at the posterior mean. Horizontal axis: quarters after the shock. Vertical axis: deviation from the steady state (inflation in pp annualised, output in \%, NFA in absolute units). The cross-country asymmetry between $\pi _F$ (German inflation, peaks at 0.04 pp) and $\pi _H$ (French inflation, peaks at 0.018 pp) quantifies the soft-inflation channel.\relax }}{7}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:irf}{{3}{7}{Impulse responses to a $+1\sigma $ German cost-push shock $\eta _{p,F}$ at the posterior mean. Horizontal axis: quarters after the shock. Vertical axis: deviation from the steady state (inflation in pp annualised, output in \%, NFA in absolute units). The cross-country asymmetry between $\pi _F$ (German inflation, peaks at 0.04 pp) and $\pi _H$ (French inflation, peaks at 0.018 pp) quantifies the soft-inflation channel.\relax }{figure.caption.10}{}}
